infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Mapped types: homomorphic vs non-homomorphic
  compares
    - label Homomorphic
      children
        - label Homomorphic: { [K in keyof T] }
          desc constraint is exactly keyof T of one parameter
        - label Preserves ? and readonly modifiers
          desc Clone keeps readonly b
        - label Preserves arrays and tuples
          desc Clone<readonly [1,2]> stays readonly [1,2]
        - label Powers Partial, Required, Readonly, Pick
    - label Non-homomorphic
      children
        - label Non-homomorphic: { [P in K] }
          desc iterates a detached key union K
        - label Modifiers are dropped
          desc no source T to copy from
        - label Arrays collapse to a plain object
          desc keys become length, push, ...
        - label Record<K,V> always yields an object
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
